  "body": "### Description\n\nafter installing synapse via snap, the home page displays a link to the matrix website that is broken:\r\n\r\nhttps://matrix.org/docs/projects/try-matrix-now.html#clients\r\n\r\ncorrect link should be:\r\n\r\nhttps://matrix.org/ecosystem/clients/\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\ninstall synapse via apt install matrix-synapse-py3\r\n\r\nvisit home page\r\n\r\nclick on incorrect link\r\n\r\nget frustrated, google \"matrix clients\"\r\n\r\nclick on correct link\n\n### Homeserver\n\nhttps://synapse.ownyourdata.site/_matrix/static/\n\n### Synapse Version\n\n{\"server_version\":\"1.86.0\",\"python_version\":\"3.10.6\"}\n\n### Installation Method\n\nOther (please mention below)\n\n### Database\n\ni don't know, irrelevant\n\n### Workers\n\nSingle process\n\n### Platform\n\nbare metal fresh install ubunutu 22.04 via `apt-get install matrix-synapse-py3 -y`\n\n### Configuration\n\n_No response_\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\nnone\n```\n\n\n### Anything else that would be useful to know?\n\nCentury Blvd. in Los Angeles was named that because it would be 100th street. seriously, look at a map.",
